WEBVTT

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.350
Well, let the Sunday Tournament begin!

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:30.310
Hurry up! Hurry up!

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.600
Who will fight first?

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:50.710
Coach, I'm really nervous about this.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.200
Joe, there you are!

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.050
Hurry up and get to the ring, the tournament is about to start!

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:10.600
I know, Nishi, but this tournament won't exactly be a walk in the park.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:14.900
For some reason, Danpei and that pansy, Aoyama, are coming for my head.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.570
But I still won't lose. Not to these guys!

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.110
Ladies and gentlemen, pleased to meet you!

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:42.390
I, Coach Tange Danpei, have humbly become the referee for this tournament.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:48.390
It's all thanks to your cooperation, my lady, that everyone's so much brighter.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:51.900
No, that's not true, all I did was sponsor them.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.510
But take a look at how lively Danpei-san is.

00:02:56.510 --> 00:03:01.360
Amateur rules will apply to all matches, so everyone should wear their head gear.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:06.370
In addition, contestants will have glove sizes assigned to match their ability.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:13.380
You'll be divided into four weight categories, with gloves of 6, 8, 10, and 12 ounces, respectively.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:19.440
This way, a punch from a strong person will equal a punch from a weaker person.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.060
This is all I have to say. Are there any questions?

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:23.890
Referee!

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.340
I agree that this glove handicap is a good idea, however,

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:33.900
I'd like to fight without head gear, given my status as a former professional boxer.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:40.400
I am not trying to look good, I simply have fairness in mind.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:48.370
I see. Given your strength, even 12 ounce gloves aren't enough, so I'll approve your request.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.390
<i>Me too!</i>

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:49.560
Me too!

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.710
I don't want a ridiculous and annoying thing like a head gear.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:52.710
<i>Joe...</i>

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:56.380
I don't give a damn about weight classes! Give me the heaviest gloves!

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.880
{HoHo...}Are you really that skilled compared to everyone else?

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:08.390
What would you know? I fought with and knocked down a former pro boxer!

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.490
Is that so? I completely forgot about that!

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:15.850
Forgot, you say!?

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.730
If you forgot then I'll have to remind you!

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.860
I'll destroy him!

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:31.460
Destroy Aoyama-kun? That won't happen!

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.310
You won't be able to do it! You definitely won't!

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:36.790
What?

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:45.720
Step aside, Joe. Everyone's waiting for the match to start.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.890
You're ruining the mood with your stupid bickering.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.390
Yeah, yeah! That's right!

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.570
There is still time before you're up.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:03.360
I suggest you observe my and Aoyama's matches and learn a thing or two.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:05.110
What!?

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.960
The gong has already rung! Get going already!

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.750
What's wrong!?

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.460
Get to the center of the ring and fight!

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:25.400
I know!

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:30.800
To face Rikiishi-san first... Great luck I have...

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:32.760
What should I do!? What should I do??

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.730
Ouch!

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:47.780
It hurts!

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:27.860
As expected from a former pro boxer, that was a fearsome punch!

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:32.310
Even with heavy gloves on, he managed to destroy the head gear strap and send his opponent flying.

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:35.870
It seems like Rikiishi-kun's greatness has reached a new level.

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:38.720
That match lasted just 16 seconds!

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:41.650
Like they say, lions show no mercy even to a hare.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:44.660
Rikiishi is one scary guy!

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:48.250
Don't make me laugh! If he can do it in sixteen seconds, I can do it in fifteen!

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:50.060
No, it wouldn't take me more than ten seconds!

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:52.890
No more than ten seconds! You listening, Nishi!?

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:56.490
I hear you, Joe, calm down! 
You don't need to be so tense.

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:58.020
I'm not tense, I'm just excited.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:04.860
I want to fight as soon as possible and show that one-eyed old man what I'm made of!

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:16.360
Hey, be careful, Matoba!

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:19.870
That Aoyama guy was trained in secret by Tange, the referee!

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:22.320
Leave it to me!

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:27.850
I still can't believe that weakling left Numata soaked in blood in the preliminaries.

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:30.880
I'll see what he's really made of.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:33.620
What are you doing, Aoyama?

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:39.390
Oh, man! Is he trying to be funny? Acting like a pro boxer!

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:46.010
He's doing that so he won't see Matoba's scary face.

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:47.300
A-Ah! I see!

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:51.900
Joe, don't you think the look in his eyes is a bit odd though?

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:52.360
His eyes?

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:57.240
Look carefully! He hasn't looked at Matoba's face, yet he keeps looking your way!

00:07:57.650 --> 00:08:01.500
Could it be that Aoyama isn't even thinking about Matoba and is already aiming for you!?

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:05.060
You're his target, Joe! You, Joe!

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:06.750
What are you trying to say, you bastard!?

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.260
Basically, Matoba isn't a problem for Aoyama.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:17.260
He's focused on his opponent for after he beats Motoba: you!

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:20.270
Focused...

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:27.310
...on me!?

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:32.580
Do your best!

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.580
<i>Don't let your guard down!</i>

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.010
Focus on your opponent!

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:35.320
All right, I've got it, shut up already!

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:43.360
Joe! Look closely, Aoyama's facial expression just changed!

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:49.340
Let's go, weakling!

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.230
He esca—

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:53.840
Where'd he go?

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:57.760
Hang in there, Matoba!

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:57.760
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.390
You're missing your target, Matoba!

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:02.810
You idiot, making a fool of me. You!

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:08.690
Where are you looking, Matoba!?

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:10.230
Stop running away!

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:18.820
Bastard!

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:23.620
What incredible footwork!

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.420
He dodged it!

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:29.580
His movement is really great!
 This is called "footwork," right, Joe?

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:35.630
I don't know for sure, but old man Danpei never taught me that.

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:43.140
Take this!

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:55.320
His agility...

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.570
He's like a runaway mouse, but...

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:00.860
No matter how perfectly he dodges, he won't get a point.

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:06.080
It's true he won't get any points, but Matoba will tire himself out.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.710
That is exactly what Aoyama is aiming for.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:10.250
Well, watch carefully.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.710
This game of cat-and-mouse will end soon. Very soon.

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:19.770
That chase lasted the whole round, yet only Matoba-san is tired!

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:25.300
Change your strategy for this guy. Watch his movements and take him down once he's tired.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:29.710
I've got it! No more chasing him around.

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:29.710
<i>Hey, look!</i>

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:32.730
Aoyama barely broke a sweat!

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.270
We're counting on you, Matoba!

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:36.740
Pay attention to your opponent!

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:42.570
It's okay if he starts moving around like a ninja again.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:45.690
I'll just wait for him to tire himself out.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:50.750
What is it?

00:10:54.350 --> 00:11:00.760
That bastard! Standing there calmly, as if he's inviting me to hit him!

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.920
Bastard!

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:06.810
What's wrong!? Both of you, fight!

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:10.650
Hey! What are you both standing around for!?

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:12.270
<i>This is no marriage interview!</i>

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:12.270
Hit him! Hit him!

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:16.540
Go, Matoba! If he's not moving then that makes it even better!

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:17.280
Go get him!

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:20.320
All right! Don't start to squirm around now!

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:21.650
You! Take this!

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:28.160
Slip! Stand up! Fight!

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:41.790
What are you doing, you dimwit!?

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:43.600
That was disgraceful, Matoba!

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:44.850
Try harder, try harder!

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.640
Aoyama's making a fool out of you!

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:57.150
Damn it, you've totally pissed me off now! Damn it!

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.650
I'll kill you. You little...

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:14.250
He's doing it again!

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:14.710
That's it!

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:18.550
That's the konjac pudding tactic that drowned Numata in a pool of blood!

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.210
This is Aoyama's specialty, the konjac tactic!

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.220
This is...

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:33.850
This is the technique he used to dodge Numata's punches.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:48.200
This is what I know so far, but what's next? What happens next!?

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.220
That Matoba guy is pitiful.

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:16.730
I guess he doesn't realize that all this swinging will wear him down much faster than usual.

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:21.730
You mean Aoyama's konjac tactic was planned?

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:26.740
You could say that. At last, the highlight of this tournament is about to start.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.210
Slip!

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.210
Stand up! Fight, fight!

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:44.260
I'm fine with the konjac tactic, but I can't stand all those missed punches anymore!

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:47.290
Show us some punch exchanges!

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:48.580
<i>Geez...</i>

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:49.260
Yeah! More punches!

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:53.040
Matoba is tired from all these misses and the audience is bored.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.330
However, it happened just like this, didn't it?

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:57.580
When Numata got beaten to the ground in his own blood!

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:58.060
Then...?

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:02.940
Konjac tactic my ass! You use tactics when you're fighting,

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:05.780
and he's not fighting, he's just running away!

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:09.070
While he can't lose like this, he also can't win!

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:15.350
It's a cowardly and unfair technique, befitting of the cowardly Aoyama!

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:28.720
Ou-Ouch. It hurts!

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:33.970
Hey! Aoyama started punching!

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:35.360
Hit him! Hit him!

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:40.000
Even so, what a lame punch! Listen to the weak-ass sound it makes!

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:54.210
This is cruel! Matoba is too tired to move, as if he's become a sandbag!

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:55.580
He's being tortured as if he's being hit by a blunt sword!

00:14:55.930 --> 00:14:58.990
Look at his face. It's swelling up pretty fast!

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:01.580
Here it is! This is how he took Numata down!

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:11.340
Whoa! The cruelty!

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:13.450
Looks like a KO to me.

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:23.150
None of his punches looked good. They were dull.

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:27.390
Yet, because his opponent was tired, any punch would be as good as a crushing blow.

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:30.750
His defense is also good. He's a completely fearsome guy!

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:38.650
That bastard! He smiled!

00:16:41.420 --> 00:16:44.810
What is it? What is it, you bastard!?

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:46.840
You've been sneakily looking at me this whole time!

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.820
If you have something to say, spit it out right here!

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:49.820
<i>Knock it off, Joe!</i>

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:57.070
Now that you've seen what Aoyama-kun can do, you realize that you can't win!

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.620
Stop kidding around!

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:04.080
You think that weird defense will work against me and my murderous punches!?

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:10.590
You imitated Rikiishi-kun with the 12 ounce gloves, yet you think you have murderous punches?

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:13.780
Unfortunately for you, the glove weight alone will beat you!

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:18.120
Before you fight Aoyama-kun, you'll be beaten up by another opponent!

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:20.810
Beaten up!?

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:26.620
This is rich!

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:31.820
What a great joke this is!

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:37.410
All right, here's a promise: If I lose, I'll walk over there naked, on my hands!

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:47.790
Why? Why is Yabuki-kun, the man who promoted the boxing club with Rikiishi-kun, being alienated?

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:53.110
He's a stray dog abandoned by his owner; barking alone, exposed to the wind.

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:54.800
That is the current state of Yabuki.

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:59.570
You'll never win if you lose your composure. That's boxing.

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:05.260
At this rate, we might actually see Yabuki walking naked on his hands.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:13.530
Matsuki, don't let your guard down!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:14.870
Yabuki is a mad dog after all!

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:17.770
He'll beat you up if you hesitate!

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:22.870
Don't worry. I was always killing stray dogs before I got sent here!

00:18:23.230 --> 00:18:25.830
You bastard, looking down on me!

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:37.050
12 ounces. These gloves are ridiculously heavy!

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:40.650
What, can't lift your gloves?

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:43.430
Want my 6 ouncers instead?

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:45.490
You bastard, don't get full of yourself.

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:47.390
You pissed me off now!

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:55.860
Damn!

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:08.370
Joe! It's useless! You'll get tired too quickly with those 12 ounce gloves!

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:23.270
Damn it! He's like a turtle hiding in his shell. I can't land a single blow.

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:25.720
And these gloves are sure heavy!

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:33.700
Joe collapsed!

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:34.690
He did it!

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:36.190
J-Joe!

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:36.970
1!

00:19:36.970 --> 00:19:38.180
2!

00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:39.190
3!

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.090
4!

00:19:40.090 --> 00:19:41.120
5!

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:41.640
6!

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:45.200
Out of the way, old man! He just got lucky!

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.200
Damn!

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:55.250
No matter how many times you punch, you won't reach me!

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:00.950
What's wrong, Joe!?

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:03.010
You having trouble with those 12 ounce gloves?

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:14.020
You should've never tried to copy Rikiishi-san when you're not even that strong!

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:16.020
You're nowhere near even his feet!

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:23.320
Down again!

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:24.250
1!

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:25.300
2!

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:26.560
3!

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:27.830
4!

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.140
5!

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:32.650
W-Wait, old man! That wasn't a knockdown! It was just a slip!

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:30.290
6!

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:32.200
7!

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:33.020
8!

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:34.070
I'm telling you, I wasn't knocked down!

00:20:34.070 --> 00:20:36.290
Stop the count! Stop it!

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:40.300
Joe! That was a knockdown! A beautiful one, too!

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:52.620
Old man, that's such a cold look. As if... 
As if you're saying, "You're going to lose."

00:20:58.080 --> 00:20:59.890
I'm getting mad now!

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:11.240
Hey, where are you going? Where are you going!?

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.830
Over here, you bastard!

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:21.000
Wait! That's a foul, Joe! It will cost you points!

00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:23.120
Take as many as you want!

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:24.050
What!?

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:27.010
Points only matter if the match is settled by points!

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:31.260
But in Yabuki Joe's battles, there's no need for points! I just need to knock him out!

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:40.110
Joe! Stop it! Stop it, Joe!

00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:42.150
That's dirty, Yabuki!

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:44.150
What do you think you're doing!?

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:44.900
Fight fair and square!

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:46.350
Stop!

00:21:46.350 --> 00:21:48.820
Foul! Minus one point!

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:49.870
Shut up!

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:53.810
Take off as many as you like!

00:22:18.470 --> 00:22:19.890
That's dirty, Yabuki!

00:22:19.890 --> 00:22:21.650
You're just fouling your opponent!

00:22:21.650 --> 00:22:25.610
Get out of the ring, Yabuki!

00:22:23.890 --> 00:22:25.610
<i>You fool! Get out!</i>

00:22:30.550 --> 00:22:31.950
He's crying!

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:37.160
That unyielding Yabuki is crying while he hits his opponent!

00:22:37.160 --> 00:22:44.630
He's acting out of desperation, like a bullied kid standing up to a bully.

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:06.240
Like hell I would lose!

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:08.150
I can't lose!

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:12.050
I just can't! Not I!

00:24:34.960 --> 00:24:39.830
Joe has worked hard and won in the first round of the prisoners' tournament.

00:24:39.830 --> 00:24:44.920
In the next match, he will face Aoyama, who I coached and taught the fearsome liver blow.

00:24:45.360 --> 00:24:47.920
Aoyama initiates a one-sided attack from the beginning of the match.

00:24:48.470 --> 00:24:52.920
Joe is completely overwhelmed.

00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:58.040
For Joe, who's cornered on the ring's ropes, which way is tomorrow!?
